<title>GERMANY: KFW agency to receive 14 bln dmks of econ package.</title>
<headline>KFW agency to receive 14 bln dmks of econ package.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government development agency Kreditanstalt fuer Wiederaufbau (KFW) will receive 14 billion marks of a government stimulus package to help the building industry, the agency said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>KFW said it would use the money in its existing credit programme for developing local infrastructure, and promoting the housing industry and mid-sized companies.</p>
<p>The total size of the government aid package announced earlier this month was 25 billion marks.</p>
<p>The agency said the government's aid package could secure up to 125,000 jobs this year in the housing industry alone and that it could protect up to 300,000 jobs in total.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
